    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0174" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6–547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-05T13:00:00+09:00">June 5, 1947—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 5—3:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1215. As supplementing Changchun’s 232, May 29 to Embassy, repeated Department as
                    1202, June 4 and Mukden’s 131, May 30, repeated Department as 78, there is
                    quoted below the latest report from Lt. Col. Cowen,<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d135-f1"/> Assistant Military Attaché at Changchun, which was
                    received at Nanking June 4: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Government 91st Division badly beaten at Kungchuling losing 2 battalions
                            either captured, surrendered or destroyed, but whole division did not
                            capitulate. Division commander was replaced. Government 88th Division
                            suffered even heavier losses in fighting between Huaiteh and
                            Kungchuling. Both divisions now reported at Ssupingkai. Changchun now
                            secure but Meihoukou almost sure to fall. Fear expressed for safety of
                            Mukden.</p>
                        <p>Comment: Doubt if Reds will withdraw to original positions unless driven
                            back which Government forces seem incapable of doing. Believe Government
                            position much worse than at any other time and unless substantial help
                            is received from China proper believe Manchuria must be lost through
                            default.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
